task_id,tier,family_id,declared_provenance,sources,license,A_citation_supports_claim,B_prefix_reproduces,C_gold_fix_resolves,D_reduction_preserves_root_cause,verdict,mechanical_detail,gate_a_evidence,gate_d_mechanism,reviewer_notes
t1_causal_mask_off_by_one,E,F1,REAL-DERIVED,https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/30095 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/36150,"Apache-2.0 (transformers) - cited as evidence only, no code copied",PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,buggy hardened=0 naive=0; gold hardened=1 naive=1,"#30095 reports _prepare_4d_attention_mask_for_sdpa being non-causal while used where causal masking is expected; #36150 reports is_causal=False having no effect. Both establish that causal-mask construction is a real, recurring defect surface in production transformer code.","Root cause preserved exactly: an off-by-one in which positions are attendable. tril(diagonal=1) grants one token of lookahead, the same class of error as the cited mask-construction defects.",
t2_rope_pairing_convention,E,F2,REAL-DERIVED,https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/25199 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/31859 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/33826,Apache-2.0 (transformers) - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,buggy hardened=0 naive=0; gold hardened=1 naive=1,"#25199 verbatim: 'This is GPT-NeoX style RoPE. But in Meta's official model implementation, the model adopts GPT-J style RoPE, which processes query and key vectors in an interleaved way instead of split into two half.' Exactly the convention mismatch our mutation introduces.","rotate_half switched from halves pairing to interleaved while the cos/sin cache still duplicates frequencies for the halves convention - the same cross-convention mismatch, at tiny scale.",
t3_rmsnorm_missing_upcast,E,F3,REAL-DERIVED,https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/35945 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/main/src/transformers/models/llama/modeling_llama.py,Apache-2.0 (transformers) - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,buggy hardened=0 naive=0; gold hardened=1 naive=1,LlamaRMSNorm upstream explicitly casts to float32 before computing the variance and back afterwards; #35945 concerns that upcast interacting badly with autocast. The upcast being load-bearing is established by the reference implementation itself.,"Removing the upcast reproduces the documented mechanism directly. Measured: fp16 x**2 exceeds 65504, variance becomes inf, rsqrt(inf)=0, output RMS collapses to exactly 0.0.",
t4_grad_accum_normalization,E,F4,REAL,https://huggingface.co/blog/gradient_accumulation | https://unsloth.ai/blog/gradient,blog posts - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,buggy hardened=0 naive=0; gold hardened=1 naive=1,"HuggingFace's own writeup documents the bug and the fix: per-micro-batch mean normalization is not equivalent to full-batch when token counts differ. Reported 2024-10-15, patched the following day, affected multi-GPU training too. This is the one task reproducing a specific documented incident verbatim.",Identical mathematics. The invariant is checkable exactly: accumulation over K micro-batches must equal one backward over the concatenation.,
t5_loss_ignore_index_dropped,E,F5,REAL-DERIVED,https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/40214 | https://huggingface.co/blog/gradient_accumulation,Apache-2.0 / blog - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,buggy hardened=0 naive=0; gold hardened=1 naive=1,"The HF writeup states the denominator is the count of non-padded, non-ignored tokens - precisely what dropping ignore_index breaks. #40214 documents padding interacting incorrectly with the objective.","ignore_index removed from cross_entropy and from the token count, so padded positions become supervised targets and the loss depends on batch composition.",
m1_attention_regression,M,F1,REAL-DERIVED,https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/30095 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/36150,Apache-2.0 - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,"buggy fails hidden=['repo_strict_causality', 'repo_matches_gold_logits']; buggy passes visible=True; gold failures=none",Same sources and reasoning as t1; only the presentation differs.,"Same root cause as t1, moved into an 8-module package with the location withheld.",
m2_position_encoding,M,F2,REAL-DERIVED,https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/25199 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/31859 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/33826,Apache-2.0 - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,"buggy fails hidden=['repo_rope_relative_property', 'repo_rope_norm_preserved', 'repo_matches_gold_logits']; buggy passes visible=True; gold failures=none","Same as t2, verbatim quote confirmed by fetching #25199.",Same mismatch as t2; symptom reduced to a downstream plateau.,
m3_gradient_lifecycle,M,F6,REAL-DERIVED,https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/optim.html | https://discuss.pytorch.org/t/zero-grad-optimizer-or-net/1887,PyTorch docs (BSD-3) / forum - evidence only,PARTIAL,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED_WITH_CAVEAT,"buggy fails hidden=['repo_gradients_reach_optimizer', 'repo_training_converges']; buggy passes visible=True; gold failures=none","The forum thread confirms the requirement -- 'We're supposed to clear the gradients each iteration before calling loss.backward() and optimizer.step()' -- and the PyTorch optim docs specify the zero_grad -> backward -> step order. But NEITHER source documents this specific failure (zero_grad landing between backward and step, producing zero-gradient updates). The pattern is real and the ordering requirement is authoritative; the incident is our construction. Recorded as PARTIAL rather than upgraded.","The violated invariant is the documented one. Measured signature: gradient norm exactly 0.0 at every optimizer step, loss 5.26 -> 5.33 over 40 steps, everything finite and warning-free.",
m4_schedule_accumulation,M,F4,REAL,https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/44511 | https://github.com/Lightning-AI/pytorch-lightning/issues/21339 | https://discuss.pytorch.org/t/userwarning-detected-call-of-lr-scheduler-step-before-optimizer-step/142833,PyTorch BSD-3 / Lightning Apache-2.0 - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,"buggy fails hidden=['repo_lr_schedule_matches_gold', 'repo_weight_decay_excludes_gains']; buggy passes visible=True; gold failures=none","PyTorch itself emits 'Detected call of lr_scheduler.step() before optimizer.step()' and documents that violating the order 'will result in PyTorch skipping the first value of the learning rate schedule'. That warning fires during this task's buggy run, so the source is not merely cited, it is triggered.","Scheduler over-stepping relative to optimizer steps, plus weight decay applied to 1-D norm gains. Measured: LR reaches 0 at step 20/40 instead of 39/40.",
m5_masking_interaction,M,F5,REAL-DERIVED,https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/40214 | https://huggingface.co/blog/gradient_accumulation,Apache-2.0 / blog - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,"buggy fails hidden=['repo_padding_does_not_change_loss', 'repo_supervised_token_count']; buggy passes visible=True; gold failures=none",Same as t5.,"Split across two modules: collate writes pad_token into label positions, and the objective counts numel(). Same root cause as t5, now requiring two coordinated edits.",
h1_attention_double_defect,H,F1,REAL-DERIVED,https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/30095 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/36150 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/40214,Apache-2.0 - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,"buggy fails hidden=['repo_strict_causality', 'repo_padding_keys_masked', 'repo_matches_gold_logits']; buggy passes visible=True; gold failures=none","Inherits m1's mask-construction evidence. The added defect (padding mask disabled) is covered by #40214, which documents padding interacting incorrectly with attention.",Two independent real defects in one file: lookahead via tril(diagonal=1) and padded keys becoming attendable. Both root causes preserved.,
h2_position_double_defect,H,F2,REAL-DERIVED,https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/25199 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/31859 | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/33826,Apache-2.0 - evidence only,PARTIAL,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED_WITH_CAVEAT,"buggy fails hidden=['repo_rope_relative_property', 'repo_rope_norm_preserved', 'repo_matches_gold_logits']; buggy passes visible=True; gold failures=none",The pairing-convention half is fully supported (#25199 verbatim). The added rope_theta 10000 -> 500 change is NOT a documented incident: it is a plausible porting error we constructed to force a two-file hypothesis. Recorded as PARTIAL rather than claimed as documented.,"Pairing mismatch preserved exactly; the frequency-base change is a second, independent position-encoding defect in a different file.",
h3_accumulation_and_clipping,H,F4,REAL,https://huggingface.co/blog/gradient_accumulation | https://unsloth.ai/blog/gradient | https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/generated/torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_.html,blog / PyTorch BSD-3 - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,"buggy fails hidden=['repo_grad_accum_matches_full_batch', 'repo_clipping_is_effective']; buggy passes visible=True; gold failures=none","The accumulation denominator defect is the verbatim October-2024 incident documented by HuggingFace. Clipping after the optimizer step contradicts the documented contract of clip_grad_norm_, which must precede the update.","Both defects preserved with their real mechanisms; measured signature is that training still learns, so neither is given away by a single number.",
h4_schedule_triple_defect,H,F4,REAL,https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/44511 | https://github.com/Lightning-AI/pytorch-lightning/issues/21339 | https://discuss.pytorch.org/t/userwarning-detected-call-of-lr-scheduler-step-before-optimizer-step/142833,PyTorch BSD-3 / Lightning Apache-2.0 - evidence only,PARTIAL,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED_WITH_CAVEAT,"buggy fails hidden=['repo_lr_schedule_matches_gold', 'repo_weight_decay_excludes_gains']; buggy passes visible=True; gold failures=none",Scheduler mis-stepping is authoritative (PyTorch emits the warning during this task's run) and weight decay on norm gains is standard practice. The third defect -- one micro-batch dropped per accumulation window -- is our construction with no specific cited incident. PARTIAL.,Three independent training-loop defects across two files; measured LR trace reaches zero at step 20/40 instead of 39/40.,
h5_masking_triple_defect,H,F5,REAL-DERIVED,https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/40214 | https://huggingface.co/blog/gradient_accumulation | https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/issues/30095,Apache-2.0 / blog - evidence only,PASS,PASS,PASS,PASS,ACCEPTED,"buggy fails hidden=['repo_supervised_token_count', 'repo_padding_does_not_change_loss', 'repo_padding_mask_reaches_model']; buggy passes visible=True; gold failures=none","Label padding and the loss denominator are covered by the HF writeup and #40214; dropping the padding mask on the training call is the same defect class as #30095/#40214, one call site further out.","Three defects spanning data -> model -> train, each preserving its own root cause; fixing any one leaves the loss batch-composition dependent.",
